      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T23:34:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e OOC, is this how modules are referenced in bp files?\n\nNot generally no as most module references do not need to select a specific APEX for a module. However, each fragment comes from a different APEX and so we need to have some way to specify the apex variant of the fragment.\n\nUsually, this reference would look something like {apex: \"com.android.bar\", module: \"bar-fragment\"} but in this case I don\u0027t specify the apex so that I can run this test in the java package instead of having to add it to the apex package.\n\n\u003e fragments: [ \":bar-fragment\" ],\n\nThat syntax is already in use and means something else which I think would be incredibly confusing. The more usual form of \"com.android.bar:bar-fragment\" might be a little less confusing, at least if you are familiar with how the bootclasspath is configured in make.\n\nHowever, while obviously, there are exceptions like \":module{tag}\" generally Colin does not like specially formatted strings in bp files. If we can come up with a better idea then it will be easy to change as there are only a few places (tests and frameworks/base) where it is used.",
      "parentUuid": "2f8b1d58_f85e8239",
